## Room 3 - Careers in Cyber

**Room Link:** https://tryhackme.com/room/careersincyber  
**Format:** Reading only (no lab)

### What It Covers

An overview of the main career paths within cybersecurity covering both offensive and defensive roles. This room is useful for orientation rather than technical learning.

**Roles covered:**

| Role | What They Do |
|------|-------------|
| Security Analyst | Monitor and protect networks; triage alerts; produce client reports |
| Security Engineer | Build and maintain security tooling and infrastructure |
| Incident Responder | Handle active security events; contain and remediate breaches |
| Digital Forensics Examiner | Collect and analyse evidence post-incident |
| Malware Analyst | Reverse engineer malicious software to understand behaviour |
| Penetration Tester | Authorised, structured attack simulation against defined targets |
| Red Teamer | Full-scale covert attack simulation testing detection and response |

The distinction between Penetration Tester and Red Teamer is worth noting. A pen tester has a defined scope and reports findings. A red teamer operates covertly across a broader attack surface specifically to test whether the blue team detects and responds correctly. The defenders are not told an exercise is happening. Different goals, different methodology.

My background sits closest to Security Analyst: SIEM monitoring, vulnerability management and client reporting. My MSc and dissertation on Monero forensics using ML points toward Digital Forensics and potentially Malware Analysis as longer-term directions.

